Find all positive integers \( n \) such that the equation \( x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = nxyz \) has integer solutions \( (x, y, z) \) where \( x, y, z \neq 0 \). Prove your solution.

Find the length of side AB in the following diagram if DE is parallel to BC, and AD = 4, DB = 12, and EC = 9.

<asy>
pair A,B,C,D,E;
A=(0,0);
B=(15,0);
C=(10,8);
D=(4,0);
E=(5,8/3);
draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(D--E);
label("$A$",A,S);
label("$B$",B,S);
label("$C$",C,N);
label("$D$",D,S);
label("$E$",E,N);
label("$4$", (A+D)/2, S);
label("$12$", (D+B)/2, S);
label("$9$", (E+C)/2, N);
</asy>

